<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa gasoline prices rise by one cent/litre.</title>
<headline>S.Africa gasoline prices rise by one cent/litre.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's Central Energy Fund said gasoline prices would rise by one cent per litre and diesel would rise by six cents with effect from May 7.</p>
<p>Illuminating paraffin would fall by four cents per litre.  </p>
<p>The Central Energy Fund said factors contributing to the adjustments included a stronger rand .</p>
<p>From May 7 the price of 93 octane gasoline in the Gauteng area around Johannesburg will be 222 cents. At the coast the price goes to 212.</p>
<p>The price of diesel in Gauteng will be 206 cents, and 196 cents on the coast, while illuminating paraffin goes to 123.53. At the coast, illuminating paraffin will be 111.43.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
